The best interval we can use (the interval whose points are given that's closest to $x=-1$) is the interval between $x=-1$ and $x=1$. Let's find the average rate of change between those points.

$\begin{align}
g'(-1)&\approx\dfrac{g(1)-g(-1)}{1-(-1)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{45-53}{2}
\\\\
&=-4
\end{align}$
